messages:
Mike (AE): FYI prospect Pegasus wants a 24h perf soak this Fri. Targets they gave: sustained 500 QPS, 2k short bursts, p99 gen <150ms non-streaming, rerank path at ~200 QPS, BYOK/HSM, SOC2. They asked for a firm cost estimate and a short runbook. Can we commit?

Sara (Sales SE): I can run ops. Proposed test profile: hybrid split (300 QPS generation, 200 QPS rerank), three prompt classes (short query ~16 tokens out, long doc ~220 tokens out, classification tiny). Ramp plan: smoke -> 0->500 over 20m -> maintain 24h -> every 6h run a 90s 2k burst. Will test model mix: rwl-small (fast) and rwl-13b-quant (throughput).

Noah (Infra Ops): We can carve Dedicated pools in us-west1 + eu-west1. Baseline for sustained load with headroom: us-west 3x A100-eq, eu-west 3x A100-eq, autoscale to +2 nodes for bursts. BYOK/HSM requires extra ops (pre-provisioning keys + network policy) and is limited to specific regions (24-48h lead).

Talia (Prod Eng): To hit p99 <150ms for generation path: prefer 13b-quant with KV prefix caching and batching. For rerank path, use smaller model but route through optimized kernel and set max_tokens=32. Suggest setting response length caps per prompt class to stabilize token cost. Note: classification workloads with small outputs will show much lower p50 but p99 depends on tail noise from batching.

Sara (Sales SE): Load generator plan: we'll run k6 in cluster mode from regional runners to avoid cross-region network noise. Example k6 snippet for generation steady state:

```js
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';

export let options = {
  vus: 500,
  duration: '10m',
};

export default function () {
  let payload = JSON.stringify({input: 'Summarize: <doc>'});
  let res = http.post('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', payload, {headers: {Authorization: 'Bearer TOKEN', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'}});
  sleep(0.02);
}
```

Sara (Sales SE): For the 2k bursts we'll spin up additional k6 runners on-demand and coordinate sync via a small orchestration script. Will push runbook and manifests by Thu EOD.

Noah (Infra Ops): Preliminary 24h cost sketch: infra (Dedicated GPUs + autoscale) ~$1,600 per region, networking & runners ~$300, ops engineering ~$700, model compute (token/GPU time) ~ $1,200 — rough total multi-region ~ $4.8k. Final line-item after average output token sizes.

sec-bot: Security questionnaire link: https://redwood.security/pegasus-sq. Required: SOC2 PDF, KMS type (CloudKMS/HSM), BYOK process doc, data residency controls, and contact for penetration test scheduling.

Mike (AE): I'll get NDA and prompt pack (incl. sample long docs) to Sara by Wed EOD. Customer prefers non-streaming and will require HSM BYOK. Can Noah confirm region availability for HSM?

Noah (Infra Ops): Confirm HSM available in us-west1; eu-west will require approval (possible delay). If they insist on BYOK in both regions, add 48h ops and small surcharge. I'll publish final costs and an ops checklist tomorrow.

Talia (Prod Eng): One final note: toggle streaming OFF and set inference timeout to 10s for the bench. That reduces p99 noise. Also we'll capture per-token latency traces & sample outputs for quality checks.

Mike (AE): Great — locking tentative run Fri 08:00 PT. Thanks team :thumbsup:
